                receive address has the same format as an ETH address and begins with "0x...", so make sure you tell
                your sender which token you want to receive and which network you want to receive it on.</p>
              <h4 class="mb-4">How to send BEP-20 tokens?</h4>
              <p>When you send a BEP-20 token, you're actually telling the token contract that a
                transfer is needed.
                The deal will demand a little amount of BNB to complete this transfer. As a result, while transmitting
                BEP-20 tokens, you use BNB as the network cost. This is why when your native BNB balance = 0, you will
                not be able to send your BEP-20 tokens from the send coin list.</p>
